Comment: The application is linked against the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the
 CardputerZero launcher by M5Stack (Copyright M5Stack Technology CO LTD, MIT) and LVGL
 (Copyright LVGL Kft, MIT), which are part of the binary and are therefore listed in
 its Copyright field below. The fonts it draws with are the launcher's, read at run
 time from /usr/share/APPLaunch/share/font (Montserrat: SIL OFL 1.1; Noto Sans CJK: SIL
 OFL 1.1, for Chinese, Japanese and Korean names); none is shipped in this package.
 .
 The V4L2 capture code, the fake camera, the conversions (including the YUV to RGB
 converter used for playback: the package does not use libswscale), the photo writer
 (EXIF and the JPEG Huffman tables of ITU-T T.81 Annex K), the recorder (the Matroska
 muxing and AAC encoding are FFmpeg's, called through its API), the journal and repair,
 the scenes list, the copy job and the pages are the app's own code, written from
 scratch for this project from the Linux V4L2 API documentation (the kernel header
 videodev2.h is used at build time only), the TurboJPEG API documentation and the
 FFmpeg API documentation. The playback engine, the outputs, the per-output volume,
 the media keys, the sound-server worker and the USB drive mounting are copied from
 the same repository's Vinyl app 0.3.0; the ALSA capture layer, the settings helpers
 (JSON, atomic writes) and the name rules from its Cassette app (same author, MIT).
 The package holds no codec code: every codec is a system library, loaded at run time.
 .
 Third-party libraries. None of the libraries below is part of this package: they are
 the system's own, provided by the OS packages named in the package's Depends field,
 which apt installs with it.
 .
 System libraries the binary is linked against at build time (named NEEDED in the
 binary): libfreetype6 (FreeType License or GPL-2.0-or-later), libinput10 (MIT),
 libxkbcommon0 (MIT), libstdc++6 and libgcc-s1 (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime
 Library Exception 3.1). They are not copied into this package.
 .
 Libraries opened at run time with dlopen, from the system; neither linked into the
 binary nor shipped in this package:
  - libturbojpeg.so.0, the TurboJPEG API of libjpeg-turbo (Copyright the libjpeg-turbo
    Project and others; IJG License, BSD-3-Clause and zlib License), to decode the
    camera's MJPEG frames for the live picture, the photos' review and MJPEG playback
    (and, for the fake camera only, to encode its test card). Package libturbojpeg0 or
    libturbojpeg.
  - FFmpeg: libavformat, libavcodec, libavutil and libswresample (Copyright the FFmpeg
    developers), to write the movies (Matroska with the camera's MJPEG frames copied
    and the microphone's sound encoded as AAC by FFmpeg's own encoder), to read them
    back for playback and the scenes' thumbnails, and to decode the sound. Opened at
    the first recording or playback, never at start-up. FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later
    upstream; Debian and Raspberry Pi OS build it with --enable-gpl, so the system
    libraries are GPL-2.0-or-later as built. Source: https://ffmpeg.org/ and the Debian
    source package "ffmpeg" (https://sources.debian.org/src/ffmpeg/). Packages
    libavformat61 (or 62), libavcodec61 (or 62), libavutil59 (or 60), libswresample5
    (or 6).
  - libasound.so.2, the ALSA library (alsa-lib, Copyright Jaroslav Kysela, Abramo
    Bagnara and others, LGPL-2.1-or-later), for the camera's microphone, the wired
    outputs and the sound card's volume control. Package libasound2t64 or libasound2.
  - libpulse.so.0, the PulseAudio and PipeWire client library (PulseAudio, Copyright
    Lennart Poettering and others, LGPL-2.1-or-later), only when a sound server runs,
    for its outputs and Bluetooth audio. Package libpulse0.
 .
 Programs run at run time when present (not dependencies): udisksctl (udisks2,
 GPL-2.0-or-later) to mount a USB drive on request and to unmount at exit the drives
 VHS mounted; vcgencmd (Raspberry Pi firmware tools) for its get_throttled flags when
 the kernel has no get_throttled node.

